  "term": "ASR",
  "definition": "ASR refers to the Adult Self-Report, a questionnaire used with adults aged 18 to 59 to gather information directly from the person about behavioral and emotional problems. In this assessment system, its results are compared with age- and sex-based norms and include scales such as internalizing, externalizing, substance use, critical items, and total problems.",
